post.description:
200 `MessageResponse`; 401 `unauthorized`; 429 `rate_limited`; 422 FastAPI's validation error for a body outside `MessageRequest`;
422 `refused` when the model declined; 503 `unavailable` when a system the reply needs could not be reached
(`RespondUnavailable`, `DevicesUnavailable`).

200 `AgreeReply`, the held calls carried out and what became of each; 401 `unauthorized`; 403 `forbidden`;
409 `gone` (carried out already, replaced by a later hold, or never held), `expired` or `not_yours` (held for
another person); 503 `unavailable`. No model is asked.

200 `BenchSummary`, the new open bench; 401 `unauthorized`; 403 `forbidden`; 422 for a body with neither title nor
ask; 503 `unavailable`. With an `ask`, her turn on it has begun by the time this answers (`api.bench_opening`);
the bench is titled by `title`, else from the ask until she names it.

SettingsRefused.description:
Why settings were not stored; nothing was. `reason`: `unknown_key`, the kind has no such setting;
`wrong_shape`, the value is not the setting's shape; `bad_id`, an id is not `domain.name` or an action is not one the
setting takes; `too_many`, a list is too long. `key` is the setting it concerns.
